## Assessment

Keep the proposal’s main direction: an application-owned project and coordinate model; a fixture-qualified OME-TIFF subset first; OME-NGFF 0.5/Zarr 3 only after pin-specific interoperability checks; a candidate napari viewing layer; local transactional metadata; and closed, versioned bundles for exchange. The proposal is unusually clear that lazy APIs, format specifications, and isolated arithmetic checks do not prove full-application memory, persistence, or export behavior. Its fallback and unsupported-input path are useful and should remain.

Before carrying this into a final proposal, make the source references correct and close several design gaps that affect the central 3 GB, identity, recovery, and export promises. These are refinements and explicit gates; they do not warrant rejecting the architecture. No application build, integration test, or performance check was run for this review. Any further validation below is **proposed / UNEXECUTED**.

